    "result": {
      "ok": true,
      "stdout": "Generate or write back an AI transition between adjacent videos.\r\n\r\nAGENT QUICKSTART (driving this as an agent? start here):\r\n  Browse commands:  lyra-cli <domain> --help\r\n\r\nUSAGE:\r\n  lyra-cli <domain> <[subdomain] ...> <action> [--flags] [--options]\r\n\r\n\r\nOPTIONS:\r\n  -h,     --help              Print this help message and exit\r\n          --ref TEXT          Unified draft reference\r\n          --after-seg-id TEXT Left video segment id; write the AI transition after this segment\r\n          --video-path TEXT   Existing AI transition product video. Omit to generate one\r\n          --effect-path TEXT  Local transition effect package path\r\n          --resource TEXT     Transition effect resource (vimo://<id> or local://<path>)\r\n          --duration <duration> \r\n                              Transition duration; explicit unit required, e.g. 1.5s\r\n          --overlap TEXT      Overlap the two segments during the transition: true / false\r\n                              (default true)\r\n          --prompt TEXT       AI transition generation prompt; required when --video-path is\r\n                              omitted\r\n          --name TEXT         Transition effect display name\r\n          --effect-id TEXT    Transition effect id\r\n          --category-id TEXT  Transition effect category id\r\n          --category-name TEXT \r\n                              Transition effect category name\r\n          --request-id TEXT   Upstream generation request id\r\n          --third-resource-id TEXT \r\n                              Third-party resource id\r\n          --task-id TEXT      Local generation task id\r\n          --source-platform TEXT \r\n                              Source platform code (int)\r\n          --skip-transtime-required TEXT \r\n                              Skip the minimum transition-time requirement: true / false\r\n                              (default false)\r\n          --poll <seconds>    Maximum whole seconds to wait for AI transition generation;\r\n                              accepts 600 or 600s (default 600 when --video-path is omitted)\r\n          --video-resolution TEXT \r\n                              Generated transition video resolution: 480p, 720p, or 1080p\r\n          --ratio TEXT        Generated transition video ratio, e.g. 16:9 or 9:16\r\n          --provider-params-json TEXT \r\n                              Provider-specific generation parameters as a JSON object or @path\r\n  -v,     --version           Show version information and exit.\r\n          --jq TEXT           Pretty-print JSON output; with an optional selector like\r\n                              .result.items[0].id, output the selected JSON value instead of\r\n                              the full schema envelope.\r\n\r\nEXAMPLES\r\n  # Generate an AI transition from adjacent boundary frames, then write it back\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft algo ai-transition \\\r\n      --prompt \"cinematic dissolve with light streaks\" \\\r\n      --effect-path /tmp/transition_effect \\\r\n      --duration 1.5s --poll 600s --after-seg-id <LEFT_UUID>\r\n  # Write an already generated AI transition product\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft algo ai-transition \\\r\n      --video-path /tmp/ai_transition.mp4 --effect-path /tmp/transition_effect \\\r\n      --duration 1.5s --after-seg-id <LEFT_UUID>\r\n  # Reference the transition effect by resource URI and overlap the two segments\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft algo ai-transition \\\r\n      --video-path /tmp/ai_transition.mp4 --resource local:///tmp/transition_effect \\\r\n      --overlap true --after-seg-id <LEFT_UUID>\r\n",
